      "side": 1,
      "message": "The tests compile using the host toolchain, both GCC and clang.\n\nAre you running into `-Wenu-conversion` errors with clang?\n\nNote that due to operator precedence, the addition operation can trigger the conversion warning.  Try this:\n\n```\nenum sensor_channel power_monitor_sensor_channel(int channel_id)\n{\n     return (enum sensor_channel)(PAC194X_CHAN_ACC1_AVG + channel_id);\n}   \n```\n\nIf still gives you problems at a minimum the return should do one final cast back to the enum type.\n\n```\nenum sensor_channel power_monitor_sensor_channel(int channel_id)\n{\n        return (enum sensor_channel)((int)PAC194X_CHAN_ACC1_AVG + channel_id);\n}   \n```",
